1
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:11,667
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:32,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:35,500
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,767 --> 00:00:41,033
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,433 --> 00:00:43,767
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,133
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:46,667
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,033 --> 00:00:51,300
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:53,633
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:55,700
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,667 --> 00:00:58,300
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:00,533
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,667 --> 00:01:02,300
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:03,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,033 --> 00:01:09,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:11,500
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,633 --> 00:01:12,733
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,867 --> 00:01:14,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:20,700
<i> Our problem's done!</i>

21
00:01:20,833 --> 00:01:22,300
<i> Mr. Chan is dead.</i>

22
00:01:22,433 --> 00:01:24,633
They can't pin it all on Victor

23
00:01:24,767 --> 00:01:26,133
<i>because their only witness
is dead.</i>

24
00:01:26,267 --> 00:01:28,300
<i>This is all the fault
of that Agent Jacinto.</i>

25
00:01:28,433 --> 00:01:30,933
<i>I won't stop
until I get my revenge.</i>

26
00:01:31,067 --> 00:01:34,167
<i>We're dealing with a
dangerous enemy.</i>

27
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:36,500
<i>We don't know
what they'll do next.</i>

28
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:37,500
<i> Be careful.</i>

29
00:01:37,633 --> 00:01:40,400
<i>If you notice
anything suspicious,</i>

30
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:41,567
<i> just call me.</i>

31
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,700
<i>Sir, suspicious character.
I'm being followed.</i>

32
00:01:43,833 --> 00:01:45,267
<i>Team, Agent Sam is
on Soriano Street.</i>

33
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,600
<i>- She needs backup.
- Are you still alive?</i>

34
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:50,167
<i>I called Domingo.
I asked him to find Sam.</i>

35
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:51,200
<i> Dad, I'll help them.</i>

36
00:01:51,333 --> 00:01:53,900
<i>Find Sam Jacinto.
Find out what happened.</i>

37
00:01:54,033 --> 00:01:55,133
<i> Her wound isn't deep.</i>

38
00:01:55,267 --> 00:01:57,533
<i>She was just grazed
by a bullet.</i>

39
00:01:57,667 --> 00:01:59,633
<i>Maybe it'll be better
if we take her to the hospital.</i>

40
00:01:59,767 --> 00:02:01,533
If we get her out of the house,

41
00:02:01,667 --> 00:02:03,567
<i>the people who are chasing her
might see her.</i>

42
00:02:04,967 --> 00:02:08,767
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,833
Why didn't you tell them
we're looking for someone?

44
00:02:10,967 --> 00:02:14,767
It'll be better if locals
help us look for her.

45
00:02:14,933 --> 00:02:17,867
Because they know every nook
and cranny of this place.

46
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,733
I don't trust them.

47
00:02:19,867 --> 00:02:21,867
They're in contact
with Boss Mariano.

48
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,467
Everyone could easily say
they know Papa.

49
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,367
We can't just believe
everyone who says so.

50
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:30,367
Harriss, Stallone,
go back in there.

51
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:31,500
Search the area.

52
00:02:31,633 --> 00:02:32,767
- Yes, boss.
- Go with them, Lee.

53
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:33,800
Sure, boss.

54
00:02:33,933 --> 00:02:36,700
We will not leave
until we find her corpse.

55
00:02:36,833 --> 00:02:37,700
Come on.

56
00:02:37,833 --> 00:02:38,800
Let's go, boys.

57
00:02:40,133 --> 00:02:41,033
[MUSIC FADES]

58
00:02:41,167 --> 00:02:46,367
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:48,733
<i>Sam isn't the only one whom
the Zafras have aggrieved.</i>

60
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,433
<i> It's an attack on me too.</i>

61
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:56,367
<i>Whatever they did
to my daughter,</i>

62
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,933
<i>I'll get back at them
10 times much.</i>

63
00:03:06,133 --> 00:03:07,067
Rudy,

64
00:03:07,967 --> 00:03:09,767
what happens tomorrow?

65
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:12,633
What will happen
if Betchay sees that woman here?

66
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:15,867
Mameng, I'm worried
about that too.

67
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:19,233
How are we going to hide her
from Betchay?

68
00:03:19,367 --> 00:03:21,133
Gabo's really something.

69
00:03:21,967 --> 00:03:24,033
Expect him to always
bring in problems at home.

70
00:03:24,167 --> 00:03:25,233
[RUDY SIGHS]

71
00:03:32,033 --> 00:03:33,167
You're so beautiful.

72
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:35,933
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

73
00:03:36,067 --> 00:03:37,433
If you ask me,

74
00:03:39,633 --> 00:03:41,867
I'm fine with you
staying here for a while.

75
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:46,767
Don't worry.

76
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:50,567
I will take care of you.

77
00:03:53,067 --> 00:03:55,400
Even though you've wronged me
a few times,

78
00:03:57,933 --> 00:03:59,400
I forgive you.

79
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,600
[SAM GRUNTS SOFTLY]

80
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:07,733
[SAM GROANING]

81
00:04:08,933 --> 00:04:10,067
[WEAKLY] It hurts.

82
00:04:11,433 --> 00:04:12,600
Miss.

83
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:14,333
[SAM GROANING]

84
00:04:14,467 --> 00:04:15,400
Miss.

85
00:04:20,967 --> 00:04:22,233
You're burning hot.

86
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:26,233
- Miss, Miss.
- [SAM BREATHING SHAKILY]

87
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:33,300
[PLASTIC RUSTLES]

88
00:04:46,533 --> 00:04:50,467
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

89
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,567
Miss.

90
00:04:53,233 --> 00:04:54,500
[SAM GROANS SOFTLY]

91
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:57,233
[GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]

92
00:04:58,333 --> 00:04:59,700
- Auntie.
- Why?

93
00:04:59,833 --> 00:05:01,033
We have a problem.

94
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:02,133
- What?
- What?

95
00:05:02,267 --> 00:05:03,467
She has a fever.

96
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:07,600
Oh no. She-- She needs ice
on her head

97
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:08,767
to lower her temperature.

98
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:11,767
Dante, go get some ice.

99
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:13,267
Just add it to the list
of how much we owe.

100
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:15,000
Hurry! Come on!

101
00:05:15,133 --> 00:05:18,000
Gabo, are we doing
the right thing?

102
00:05:18,133 --> 00:05:21,200
Maybe it'll be better
to take her to the hospital.

103
00:05:21,333 --> 00:05:22,600
But, Auntie,

104
00:05:22,733 --> 00:05:24,900
it's too dangerous to do that.

105
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:26,800
We don't know
who she's running away from.

106
00:05:26,933 --> 00:05:28,933
If we get her out of the house,

107
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:30,600
her enemies might see.

108
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:34,800
It's better if we do
everything we can for now.

109
00:05:34,967 --> 00:05:37,567
Damn it, what if
she gets worse while in here?

110
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:39,000
Here's the ice.

111
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,500
Oh god, you poor thing.

112
00:05:55,667 --> 00:05:57,200
Don't worry.

113
00:05:57,333 --> 00:06:00,667
We will take care
of you here, okay?

114
00:06:02,767 --> 00:06:05,367
This is going to be cold.
i'm sorry.

115
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:08,967
I know you're cold
but you need this.

116
00:06:09,133 --> 00:06:10,767
Have you known Ma'am
for a long time?

117
00:06:11,767 --> 00:06:12,833
Why are you asking?

118
00:06:12,967 --> 00:06:14,167
I just want to know.

119
00:06:15,467 --> 00:06:16,900
How did you two meet?

120
00:06:17,633 --> 00:06:18,767
How about you?

121
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:22,667
Have you been working for
the Zafras for a long time?

122
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,433
A long, long time.

123
00:06:26,933 --> 00:06:30,700
I just want to know if
the group can really trust you.

124
00:06:31,667 --> 00:06:33,467
I will not answer your
questions.

125
00:06:34,267 --> 00:06:36,000
Because you're not my boss.

126
00:06:38,267 --> 00:06:39,467
And I don't think

127
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,567
you'll be of any use to me.

128
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:46,300
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:06:46,433 --> 00:06:47,400
Gabo.

130
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:50,400
Isn't it more dangerous
that she's here?

131
00:06:50,533 --> 00:06:51,733
If she got shot,

132
00:06:51,867 --> 00:06:54,433
the people chasing her
probably have guns.

133
00:06:54,567 --> 00:06:55,467
It's risky for us too.

134
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,267
They could be firing bullets
at us anytime!

135
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:58,333
Uncle,

136
00:06:58,467 --> 00:06:59,833
there is nothing else we can do.

137
00:07:00,567 --> 00:07:02,700
What matters now
is saving her life.

138
00:07:04,967 --> 00:07:06,700
You know what,

139
00:07:06,833 --> 00:07:07,833
Gabo is right.

140
00:07:08,833 --> 00:07:10,533
If something bad happens
to that woman,

141
00:07:10,667 --> 00:07:12,200
guilt will eat us up.

142
00:07:12,333 --> 00:07:15,133
Pa, as a matter of fact,

143
00:07:16,167 --> 00:07:17,500
that woman is my mortal enemy.

144
00:07:17,633 --> 00:07:19,700
We've encountered
each other twice.

145
00:07:19,833 --> 00:07:22,200
The first time
was when I got out of jail.

146
00:07:22,333 --> 00:07:24,967
I saved people from
a robbery incident on a bus.

147
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:27,067
And then she came to help.

148
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:28,533
She kissed me then slapped me!

149
00:07:29,467 --> 00:07:31,867
The second time was at the bar.

150
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,400
She pushed me
and almost slapped me again.

151
00:07:33,533 --> 00:07:35,733
Jeez.
That woman is tough.

152
00:07:35,867 --> 00:07:37,967
What does she have
against you?

153
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:40,467
What if she wakes up

154
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,167
and gets back at you?

155
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:44,233
She's an NCIA agent!

156
00:07:45,767 --> 00:07:46,900
Pa...

157
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:51,500
The only thing that matters now
is keeping her safe.

158
00:07:51,667 --> 00:07:56,200
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

159
00:07:56,333 --> 00:08:00,667
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

160
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:03,833
[SIRENS WAILING]

161
00:08:03,967 --> 00:08:05,167
[TIRES SCREECH]

162
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:07,200
[TIRES SCREECH]

163
00:08:11,233 --> 00:08:14,167
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

164
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:15,700
Stop what you're doing!

165
00:08:15,833 --> 00:08:19,733
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

166
00:08:19,867 --> 00:08:21,367
[RADIO CHATTER]

167
00:08:23,033 --> 00:08:25,200
We're NCIA agents.

168
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:27,067
- You're from the NCIA?
- Yes.

169
00:08:27,967 --> 00:08:30,033
This is NLEA jurisdiction.

170
00:08:30,167 --> 00:08:32,000
One of our colleagues
was involved in the ambush.

171
00:08:32,133 --> 00:08:33,167
And we arrived first.

172
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:34,767
It doesn't matter.

173
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:36,000
This is a crime scene,

174
00:08:36,133 --> 00:08:37,500
and it's our job
to investigate it.

175
00:08:37,633 --> 00:08:38,900
[SEQIOA] For the last time,

176
00:08:39,033 --> 00:08:42,733
we're here because this incident
involves an NCIA agent.

177
00:08:42,867 --> 00:08:44,567
Was I talking to you?

178
00:08:45,467 --> 00:08:46,767
Watch it, man.

179
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:47,800
You don't want this.

180
00:08:47,933 --> 00:08:54,800
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

181
00:08:54,967 --> 00:08:56,833
[RADIO CHATTER]

182
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:06,400
You don't get to come
into our turf

183
00:09:06,533 --> 00:09:10,300
poke around,
and then claim the case.

184
00:09:10,433 --> 00:09:12,567
We're not here to
claim your case.

185
00:09:13,433 --> 00:09:15,833
We're just looking
for our colleague.

186
00:09:15,967 --> 00:09:18,500
[ESTRELLA]
So what did you find?

187
00:09:20,867 --> 00:09:22,233
The car was abandoned.

188
00:09:22,367 --> 00:09:24,300
Multiple bullet impacts.

189
00:09:24,433 --> 00:09:25,733
Five fatalities.

190
00:09:25,867 --> 00:09:27,767
But Agent Sam is missing.

191
00:09:27,933 --> 00:09:30,367
We believe
she made it out alive.

192
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:32,100
It's possible.

193
00:09:32,233 --> 00:09:33,267
It is.

194
00:09:34,267 --> 00:09:35,667
Because we didn't
recover a body

195
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:38,233
or even a trace of blood
on the driver's seat.

196
00:09:38,367 --> 00:09:39,400
[SCOFFS]

197
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:41,167
All right.

198
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:43,000
Leave the scene.
We'll take it from here.

199
00:09:43,133 --> 00:09:44,700
- Men!
- We can't let you do that.

200
00:09:44,833 --> 00:09:51,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

201
00:09:51,467 --> 00:09:53,000
This is connected

202
00:09:53,133 --> 00:09:55,433
to our operation
targeting the Zafras.

203
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:59,700
If that's the case,
then we have a problem.

204
00:09:59,833 --> 00:10:00,733
That's up to you.

205
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:07,867
[TENSE MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

206
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,467
Excuse me.

207
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:24,367
Have you noticed
a woman in a red jacket?

208
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,500
No, sir.

209
00:10:32,767 --> 00:10:34,833
I've wiped her down
with a cold towel.

210
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,900
Her temperature
is starting to drop.

211
00:10:37,033 --> 00:10:39,067
I hope her fever goes down next.

212
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:45,400
- [DOGS BARKING]
- [UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

213
00:10:45,533 --> 00:10:46,500
What's going on?

214
00:10:46,633 --> 00:10:49,533
[BARKING CONTINUES]

215
00:10:54,133 --> 00:11:01,067
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

216
00:11:01,633 --> 00:11:03,733
Gabo, who are those men?

217
00:11:03,867 --> 00:11:05,033
I don't know, Pa.

218
00:11:06,633 --> 00:11:08,133
They're not from here.

219
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:11,667
Auntie!
Turn the lights off!

220
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:14,433
- [LIGHT SWITCH CLICKS]
- [DOG HOWLS, BARKS]

221
00:11:15,667 --> 00:11:17,700
Pa, I'm going out.

222
00:11:17,833 --> 00:11:18,633
Stay here.

223
00:11:18,767 --> 00:11:20,300
[DANTE] Gabo!
You can't go out!

224
00:11:20,433 --> 00:11:23,767
They might find out
that woman is here!

225
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:25,533
- They might hurt you!
- [MAMENG] Shh!

226
00:11:25,667 --> 00:11:26,633
Keep it down!

227
00:11:26,767 --> 00:11:28,100
I'll deal with them.

228
00:11:28,233 --> 00:11:34,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

229
00:11:34,433 --> 00:11:38,300
Don't worry.
I'll protect you.

230
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:45,833
[RUDY] Gabo!

231
00:11:45,967 --> 00:11:47,167
Just stay here!

232
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:48,833
I got this, Pa.

233
00:11:48,967 --> 00:11:50,333
Stay here.

234
00:11:50,467 --> 00:11:51,600
Do not go outside.

235
00:11:52,267 --> 00:11:53,267
Gabo!

236
00:11:53,400 --> 00:12:00,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

237
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:11,433
Anything?

238
00:12:12,867 --> 00:12:14,133
Can I help you, gentlemen?

239
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:20,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

240
00:12:20,433 --> 00:12:22,067
In our neighborhood,

241
00:12:24,433 --> 00:12:26,133
strangers who come here...

242
00:12:27,767 --> 00:12:29,633
don't make it out alive.

243
00:12:30,867 --> 00:12:32,600
I don't recognize any of you.

244
00:12:32,733 --> 00:12:34,233
What brings you here?

245
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:36,433
That's none of your business!

246
00:12:37,867 --> 00:12:38,700
Dante!

247
00:12:38,833 --> 00:12:40,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

248
00:12:42,467 --> 00:12:46,467
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

249
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:49,467
[MAX] Sir!

250
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:56,133
Sir, have you found Sam?

251
00:12:56,133 --> 00:12:58,233
Ma'am, we still haven't found
your sister.

252
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:01,700
Don't worry, Max.

253
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:03,667
I'll make sure we stay
on top of this case.

254
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:06,700
[CASTOR] Ma'am,
I know Sam's your sister.

255
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:09,000
But this is our operation
against the Zafras.

256
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
We have clearance
to handle this case.

257
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,767
It came from General Jacinto.

258
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:18,800
Maybe the NCIA and NLEA
can work together on this.

259
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:19,867
No.

260
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,433
I'm handling this case.

261
00:13:22,467 --> 00:13:24,133
I was given clearance for it.

262
00:13:25,333 --> 00:13:26,967
The NLEA will handle it.

263
00:13:26,967 --> 00:13:29,933
The NCIA operation
is what led to the ambushes.

264
00:13:29,933 --> 00:13:31,467
These bodies?

265
00:13:31,467 --> 00:13:33,367
They could be Zafra men.

266
00:13:33,367 --> 00:13:36,033
And Sam arrested Victor Zafra.

267
00:13:36,467 --> 00:13:38,367
This wasn't an ordinary ambush.

268
00:13:38,367 --> 00:13:41,267
The Zafras are retaliating
against the NCIA.

269
00:13:41,267 --> 00:13:42,867
And Sam's their target.

270
00:13:42,867 --> 00:13:44,267
Stop arguing!

271
00:13:44,267 --> 00:13:46,467
Fine.
Do your own investigation, then.

272
00:13:46,467 --> 00:13:48,300
I'm not doing this
as an NLEA officer.

273
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,433
I'm doing this because
Sam's my sister.

274
00:13:53,667 --> 00:13:54,967
- Excuse me.
- Ma'am.

275
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,200
[SIRENS WAILING]

276
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,567
- Go with her.
- Medina, go with her!

277
00:14:01,733 --> 00:14:08,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

278
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,300
[MUSIC FADES]

279
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,400
Bro...

280
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:19,200
You've got some guts, huh?

281
00:14:20,333 --> 00:14:22,467
You got no idea
where you just walked into.

282
00:14:24,367 --> 00:14:26,100
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

283
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:27,600
Neighbors!

284
00:14:30,133 --> 00:14:31,633
We've got outsiders!

285
00:14:31,633 --> 00:14:33,367
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

286
00:14:33,367 --> 00:14:35,133
- Who are you?
- You're pretty brave!

287
00:14:35,133 --> 00:14:37,867
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

288
00:14:37,867 --> 00:14:40,200
You picked the wrong place
to come into.

289
00:14:41,333 --> 00:14:44,767
Bro, you're getting too brave.

290
00:14:46,567 --> 00:14:49,367
Even if you fire that gun
and kill me here,

291
00:14:50,967 --> 00:14:52,167
you're only four.

292
00:14:54,367 --> 00:14:55,833
I can assure you,

293
00:14:56,667 --> 00:14:59,367
you won't make it
out of here alive.

294
00:14:59,367 --> 00:15:01,333
Bro, sorry.

295
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:04,200
We're just looking for someone.

296
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:07,067
If my men didn't see anyone,
we'll leave!

297
00:15:07,433 --> 00:15:09,200
- Leave!
- What are you waiting for?

298
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,900
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

299
00:15:10,900 --> 00:15:12,100
Men, let's go!

300
00:15:12,100 --> 00:15:13,200
- Leave!
- Go!

301
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:14,600
[DANTE] What a bunch of cowards.

302
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:16,067
- Leave!
- Don't come back!

303
00:15:17,433 --> 00:15:19,900
Gabo, who were those guys?
Why were they here?

304
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:26,233
I don't know them.

305
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,233
They're looking for
some snatchers.

306
00:15:29,767 --> 00:15:31,600
That's why they came
to our neighborhood.

307
00:15:32,833 --> 00:15:34,733
- Go on. Get some rest.
- Okay.

308
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:36,833
- Come on! Come on!
- Let's go!

309
00:15:36,833 --> 00:15:38,233
Gabo, come inside.

310
00:15:38,233 --> 00:15:40,033
- They might come back.
- [MAMENG] Gabo!

311
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:43,000
You guys are unbelievable!

312
00:15:43,567 --> 00:15:45,867
Gabo, you shouldn't have
gone out there.

313
00:15:45,867 --> 00:15:47,900
You're going to get us
caught up in this mess!

314
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:50,200
Good grief, you're going
to give me a heart attack!

315
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:53,133
Auntie, we'd be more involved
if I did nothing.

316
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:55,767
I just made it clear to them

317
00:15:55,767 --> 00:15:58,500
that they can't just barge
into our neighborhood!

318
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:02,167
So they'd know who lives here

319
00:16:02,167 --> 00:16:03,867
and what kind of place this is!

320
00:16:03,867 --> 00:16:06,133
Gabo, let's just get some sleep.

321
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:09,567
Dante, lock all the doors, okay?

322
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:11,300
Come on, babes. Let's go inside.

323
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:12,633
Don't call me "babes"!

324
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,000
You're acting all tough.

325
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,133
Didn't you see they were
younger than you?

326
00:16:17,133 --> 00:16:18,700
And you still went out there!

327
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:24,767
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:27,433
[MAN] Come on, bottoms up.

329
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:30,333
Ma'am, Sir Umali sent us
to follow you.

330
00:16:30,333 --> 00:16:32,233
Okay. Search that area.

331
00:16:32,233 --> 00:16:33,400
Yes, ma'am! Let's go!

332
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:34,600
Estrella, this way.

333
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:36,400
Hey, looks like
we've got company.

334
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:38,333
- [MAX] Good evening!
- What is it, ma'am?

335
00:16:38,333 --> 00:16:40,500
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

336
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,600
Did you notice
an injured woman here?

337
00:16:43,167 --> 00:16:44,667
And some armed men?

338
00:16:44,667 --> 00:16:46,567
No, ma'am.
We only heard the gunshots,

339
00:16:46,567 --> 00:16:47,867
but we didn't go outside.

340
00:16:47,867 --> 00:16:49,500
Don't you have CCTV here?

341
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:51,067
There's only one
CCTV camera here,

342
00:16:51,067 --> 00:16:52,200
but it isn't working.

343
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:54,067
Don't you know
where the shooters went?

344
00:16:54,067 --> 00:16:57,967
No, ma'am. Maybe you should
check another barangay.

345
00:16:57,967 --> 00:16:59,567
You might find them there.

346
00:16:59,567 --> 00:17:00,733
Thanks anyway.

347
00:17:02,067 --> 00:17:03,233
Estrella, let's go.

348
00:17:04,167 --> 00:17:05,600
[MAN] Come on, bottoms up again.

349
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:08,400
Max, let's go back
to the station for now.

350
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:10,100
I still haven't found Sam!

351
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:11,567
I'll leave some of my men here.

352
00:17:11,567 --> 00:17:13,467
They'll continue
the investigation.

353
00:17:13,467 --> 00:17:14,633
Come on.

354
00:17:16,100 --> 00:17:17,400
Get some rest, ma'am.

355
00:17:18,033 --> 00:17:22,067
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

356
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,067
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

357
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:34,467
Poor thing.

358
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:38,467
I hope your fever
goes down soon.

359
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:41,000
Don't worry.

360
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,400
They won't get you.

361
00:17:44,933 --> 00:17:47,000
I'm here to protect you.

362
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:52,367
I'd risk my life for you.

363
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:58,167
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

364
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:07,367
Whoever's trying to kill you,

365
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:11,700
I promise you...

366
00:18:13,967 --> 00:18:15,467
they won't succeed.

367
00:18:16,567 --> 00:18:23,400
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

368
00:18:33,333 --> 00:18:34,633
Umali.

369
00:18:34,633 --> 00:18:35,800
Any news?

370
00:18:36,733 --> 00:18:38,933
- Sir.
- Jacinto, you're here.

371
00:18:38,933 --> 00:18:41,100
I'm helping search
for my sister.

372
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:43,100
This is General Jacinto's
daughter.

373
00:18:43,967 --> 00:18:45,433
The NLEA will do
everything it can

374
00:18:45,433 --> 00:18:47,033
to find your sister.

375
00:18:47,033 --> 00:18:48,867
So don't worry.
Not on my watch.

376
00:18:48,867 --> 00:18:51,067
Sir, permission to form
a task force

377
00:18:51,067 --> 00:18:53,333
to speed up the search for Sam.

378
00:18:53,333 --> 00:18:54,533
Do what you need to do.

379
00:18:54,533 --> 00:18:55,833
Thank you, sir.

380
00:18:55,867 --> 00:18:57,067
Excuse me.

381
00:18:57,067 --> 00:19:00,833
[SIRENS WAILING]

382
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:08,967
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

383
00:19:16,067 --> 00:19:18,333
This is all your fault, Ricardo.

384
00:19:18,733 --> 00:19:20,033
How is this my fault?

385
00:19:20,767 --> 00:19:24,967
You let Sam join the NCIA.

386
00:19:24,967 --> 00:19:27,967
This isn't what I wanted
for my daughter!

387
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,100
What mother would ever want
her children

388
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:33,500
in a job that could
get them killed?

389
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,200
Look what's happening!

390
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:38,433
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

391
00:19:38,433 --> 00:19:40,967
No one forced her
to join the NCIA.

392
00:19:44,367 --> 00:19:45,800
She did it because...

393
00:19:47,467 --> 00:19:49,567
because she wanted
to make it up to the family

394
00:19:49,567 --> 00:19:50,733
for what she'd done.

395
00:19:50,733 --> 00:19:54,067
You never should've let her
into your world!

396
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:57,033
None of this would've happened!

397
00:19:57,033 --> 00:20:00,033
Ricardo, I've already lost
one child!

398
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:06,000
I can't bear to lose another!

399
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:12,867
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

400
00:20:28,167 --> 00:20:29,867
Estrella, you should go home.

401
00:20:29,867 --> 00:20:32,733
It's fine even if
I don't have news to give Dad.

402
00:20:32,733 --> 00:20:35,467
We did the best we could,
didn't we, ma'am?

403
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:38,767
We did our best,
but we still can't find Sam!

404
00:20:38,767 --> 00:20:42,000
Ma'am, based on your stories
about your sister...

405
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:46,700
I know that
Ma'am Sam can protect herself.

406
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:48,567
Wherever she may be.

407
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:50,967
After all, she's a Jacinto.

408
00:20:52,133 --> 00:20:53,967
She's strong.
She can protect herself!

409
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:56,867
I'm sure of that.

410
00:20:58,733 --> 00:21:00,467
Thank you, Estrella.

411
00:21:02,967 --> 00:21:04,867
There's only one thing
I can pray for now...

412
00:21:07,367 --> 00:21:10,300
I pray my sister
is far away from danger.

413
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:21,733
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

414
00:21:24,967 --> 00:21:26,633
- [POLICE] Sir.
- At ease, men.

415
00:21:28,167 --> 00:21:31,800
[PHONE RINGING]

416
00:21:33,367 --> 00:21:35,167
- General Jacinto.
- Domingo.

417
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:38,433
You haven't even given me
an update!

418
00:21:38,433 --> 00:21:41,267
General, our search
is still ongoing.

419
00:21:41,267 --> 00:21:42,300
[RICARDO] Ongoing?

420
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:45,167
So that means
you haven't found her.

421
00:21:46,067 --> 00:21:49,300
Domingo, are you forgetting
who put you in that position?

422
00:21:49,300 --> 00:21:51,467
I have not forgotten, General.

423
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,233
Well, that's good.

424
00:21:53,233 --> 00:21:55,367
But, so far,
you've been useless to me!

425
00:21:57,867 --> 00:22:01,167
Don't rest
until you find Samantha.

426
00:22:02,833 --> 00:22:05,933
- Yes--
- [LINE DROPS]

427
00:22:08,433 --> 00:22:09,533
[PHONE THUDS]

428
00:22:14,733 --> 00:22:19,233
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

429
00:22:19,267 --> 00:22:20,567
- [LOUD THUD]
- Sir!

430
00:22:21,300 --> 00:22:22,300
[SANTOS] Sir.

431
00:22:24,100 --> 00:22:25,200
[SANTOS CLEARS THROAT]

432
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:28,800
Did you look
for Detective Sam Jacinto?

433
00:22:30,533 --> 00:22:35,000
She's not just any
other person, you understand?

434
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:38,100
General Jacinto's daughter
is missing!

435
00:22:39,567 --> 00:22:42,933
[SANTOS] Colonel,
we didn't stop from searching.

436
00:22:43,533 --> 00:22:45,533
- What?
- Actually,

437
00:22:45,533 --> 00:22:47,700
we lost sleep
from looking for her.

438
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:50,967
Besides, sir, we did our best.

439
00:22:51,867 --> 00:22:53,033
[DOMINGO] Your best?

440
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:57,400
You tried your best,
but I'm not seeing any results!

441
00:22:58,033 --> 00:23:03,100
Where did Sam Jacinto go?
Is Sam Jacinto still alive?!

442
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:05,133
Do you know anything at all?!

443
00:23:06,367 --> 00:23:10,267
Sir, we'll soon find out
who did this.

444
00:23:11,133 --> 00:23:14,000
And we will soon find
Sam Jacinto.

445
00:23:14,700 --> 00:23:17,133
And whoever did this
to Sam Jacinto,

446
00:23:17,133 --> 00:23:18,900
we'll make them pay.

447
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:27,300
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

448
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:49,367
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

449
00:23:51,233 --> 00:23:52,300
[DOOR OPENS]

450
00:23:53,500 --> 00:23:56,833
Boss, this is the address
of the Zafras.

451
00:23:58,267 --> 00:24:04,200
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

452
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:06,133
- [DRAWER SLIDES]
- [CASE RATTLES]

453
00:24:08,300 --> 00:24:09,300
[CASE THUDS]

454
00:24:11,433 --> 00:24:12,933
If they don't give us Sam...

455
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:15,033
[GUN COCKS]

456
00:24:15,033 --> 00:24:18,667
We'll get her back
by whatever means necessary.

457
00:24:18,667 --> 00:24:19,733
Yes, boss.

458
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,333
[DOOR OPENS, CREAKS]

459
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:27,700
Arturo, did Lucas come home
last night?

460
00:24:27,700 --> 00:24:28,667
No, ma'am.

461
00:24:37,500 --> 00:24:39,367
Why would you call Lucas?

462
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:43,800
To make him go home.
He's had a long night.

463
00:24:47,433 --> 00:24:50,567
He has to finish
what I ordered him to do.

464
00:24:52,633 --> 00:24:55,800
Which is
to find Samantha Jacinto's body.

465
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:58,567
If you want to prove that
your child is now capable...

466
00:25:00,367 --> 00:25:02,267
...then don't coddle him.

467
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:07,767
- I'll do it.
- I keep repeating--

468
00:25:07,767 --> 00:25:09,467
- Max.
- [MAX] Ma.

469
00:25:09,467 --> 00:25:11,867
You spent the night at work.
What happened?

470
00:25:11,867 --> 00:25:13,633
Did they find Sam?

471
00:25:13,633 --> 00:25:16,200
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

472
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:17,833
[ISOBEL SIGHS] My god.

473
00:25:17,833 --> 00:25:18,867
Not yet, Ma.

474
00:25:22,133 --> 00:25:23,133
Toto!

475
00:25:24,833 --> 00:25:27,067
- Sir!
- Get the car ready.

476
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:29,867
- Manny, get our men ready.
- Yes, boss.

477
00:25:29,867 --> 00:25:33,133
- W-Where will we go, sir?
- We'll visit someone.

478
00:25:33,133 --> 00:25:35,167
- [TOTO] Sweetie. Hold this.
- Toto.

479
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:37,767
What's with you, Toto?
You keep moving!

480
00:25:37,767 --> 00:25:40,133
- It's sir!
- What's going on?

481
00:25:40,133 --> 00:25:42,167
S-Sir is asking
to get the car ready.

482
00:25:42,167 --> 00:25:43,700
We're visiting someone.

483
00:25:43,700 --> 00:25:46,267
- You know what that means.
- What do you mean?

484
00:25:46,267 --> 00:25:47,267
Huh?!

485
00:25:47,933 --> 00:25:51,300
Ricardo! Ricardo,
what's happening?

486
00:25:51,300 --> 00:25:54,233
Boss, our men are armed
and ready.

487
00:25:54,233 --> 00:25:55,900
What do you mean
your men are armed?

488
00:25:55,900 --> 00:25:57,067
- What are you talking--
- [RICARDO] Isobel.

489
00:25:57,067 --> 00:25:59,100
I will make sure
Sam comes home.

490
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:01,233
- I'll come with you.
- [RICARDO] Stay here.

491
00:26:01,233 --> 00:26:02,933
- No!
- [RICARDO] Stay here!

492
00:26:02,933 --> 00:26:04,333
Mom.

493
00:26:04,333 --> 00:26:06,767
Ma! You just have to trust Dad.

494
00:26:06,767 --> 00:26:09,600
[WHIMPERS] But Sam...

495
00:26:10,500 --> 00:26:13,967
What's gonna happen
to our visitor?

496
00:26:14,800 --> 00:26:17,500
We can't keep her here forever!

497
00:26:17,500 --> 00:26:20,867
And she's even an NCIA agent!

498
00:26:20,867 --> 00:26:24,233
What if someone's looking
for her?

499
00:26:24,233 --> 00:26:28,133
We might get dragged
into the mess she escaped from!

500
00:26:28,133 --> 00:26:29,167
No, wait.

501
00:26:29,933 --> 00:26:31,767
I already talked to Gabo.

502
00:26:31,767 --> 00:26:36,500
Once that woman recovers,
he'll help her get out of here.

503
00:26:36,500 --> 00:26:39,933
I can understand
Gabo's kindness.

504
00:26:39,933 --> 00:26:41,733
It's not wrong to help.

505
00:26:41,733 --> 00:26:44,167
But we might get into danger!

506
00:26:44,833 --> 00:26:47,333
Gabo won't put us in danger.

507
00:26:48,100 --> 00:26:50,133
Besides, the woman's wounds
aren't that bad.

508
00:26:50,900 --> 00:26:52,800
Let's just let her recover
for now.

509
00:26:55,067 --> 00:26:57,900
- Pa.
- Gabo! How is she?

510
00:26:57,900 --> 00:27:01,400
[GABO] I think
her condition is improving.

511
00:27:10,033 --> 00:27:11,167
There was a shootout last night!

512
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:12,633
- Huh?
- That's why there were men

513
00:27:12,767 --> 00:27:14,700
searching the neighborhood
last night.

514
00:27:14,833 --> 00:27:16,133
- Really?
- What? Who were they?

515
00:27:16,300 --> 00:27:18,333
- Who were they looking for?
- Did they mention a name?

516
00:27:18,467 --> 00:27:21,500
I-I was too scared
to ask them.

517
00:27:21,633 --> 00:27:24,333
All I know is
they're looking for someone.

518
00:27:24,467 --> 00:27:25,767
- Maybe it's--
- Shh!

519
00:27:25,900 --> 00:27:27,933
- Shut up!
- Your spit hit me!

520
00:27:28,067 --> 00:27:30,000
- Shut it.
- All right. Come on.

521
00:27:30,133 --> 00:27:31,600
Enough gossip.

522
00:27:31,733 --> 00:27:34,100
- Gossipers.
- Who could it be?

523
00:27:34,233 --> 00:27:36,733
<i>- Gabo?
- Who could it be?</i>

524
00:27:36,867 --> 00:27:37,900
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN]

525
00:27:39,300 --> 00:27:40,700
- Gabo.
- Gabo.

526
00:27:40,833 --> 00:27:44,100
Gabo, there are men
circling our neighborhood.

527
00:27:44,233 --> 00:27:45,600
They're looking for someone.

528
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:48,133
Are they looking for you?

529
00:27:48,267 --> 00:27:50,800
[TEKLA] Gabo, did something
happen yesterday?

530
00:27:50,967 --> 00:27:54,067
[BONG] Just say the word, Gabo.
We've got your back

531
00:27:54,200 --> 00:27:55,900
We're ready to fight.

532
00:27:56,033 --> 00:27:58,633
I have something
important to tell you.

533
00:27:58,767 --> 00:28:02,600
But this has to stay between us.

534
00:28:03,433 --> 00:28:04,633
Let's talk outside.

535
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:07,967
Come on.

536
00:28:09,367 --> 00:28:16,333
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

537
00:28:17,100 --> 00:28:18,633
[DOG BARKING]

538
00:28:20,733 --> 00:28:21,633
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

539
00:28:21,800 --> 00:28:28,767
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

540
00:28:34,533 --> 00:28:36,567
<i> Our men are armed and ready.</i>

541
00:28:36,700 --> 00:28:38,733
<i>I will make sure
Sam comes home.</i>

542
00:28:38,867 --> 00:28:39,833
<i> Do you remember</i>

543
00:28:39,967 --> 00:28:42,567
<i>the NCIA agent I faced
in our first mission?</i>

544
00:28:42,700 --> 00:28:43,733
<i> That fair-skinned woman?</i>

545
00:28:43,867 --> 00:28:46,967
<i>I heard there was
a shootout here last night.</i>

546
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:48,033
<i> What happened?</i>

547
00:28:48,167 --> 00:28:49,400
<i> Mama Betchay can't know.</i>

548
00:28:49,533 --> 00:28:51,067
<i>We don't want Paquito
getting wind of this.</i>

549
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:53,267
<i>If that happens, they'll
definitely find her here.</i>

550
00:28:54,667 --> 00:28:58,633
<i>What if Betchay told Gabo
and Rudy about our plans?</i>

551
00:28:58,800 --> 00:29:01,167
<i> I know women like her.</i>

552
00:29:01,300 --> 00:29:04,300
<i>They'll side with
whoever pays them.</i>

553
00:29:04,433 --> 00:29:05,867
- [GRUNTS] Put your gun down!
- Who are you?

554
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:08,167
<i>- You might shoot me.
- I will shoot you!</i>

555
00:29:08,300 --> 00:29:09,233
- [GABO GRUNTS]
<i> - Gabo!</i>

556
00:29:09,367 --> 00:29:11,567
<i>What am I doing here?!
Why am I here?!</i>

557
00:29:11,700 --> 00:29:12,500
<i> Who is that?</i>

558
00:29:12,633 --> 00:29:14,133
<i>Pipe it down!
I'm trying to sleep!</i>

559
00:29:14,133 --> 00:29:15,033
<i> Who am I?</i>

560
00:29:15,167 --> 00:29:16,800
<i>Love!
Your name is Gloria.</i>

561
00:29:16,933 --> 00:29:18,333
<i> I'm your husband, Gabo.</i>

562
00:29:18,467 --> 00:29:19,767
<i> Can you please shut up?</i>

563
00:29:19,900 --> 00:29:21,500
<i> Husband? You're my husband?</i>

564
00:29:21,633 --> 00:29:23,300
<i> Don't make me count to three!</i>

565
00:29:23,433 --> 00:29:24,500
<i> My love...</i>
